# as reproduced in the archived Wikipedia article 'Effective nuclear charge'
# (https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Effective_nuclear_charge&oldid=712358437).
#
# Correction vs the Wikipedia transcription: Kr (Z=36) 2p is 32.047, not 26.047 -- the page
# value breaks the monotone sequence (Br 2p 31.056, Rb 2p 33.039) and is a typo of the 1963
# table (the page itself is a transcription of it).
#
# Keys: Z -> {(n, l): Z_eff}. Values correspond to the real Hartree-Fock ground-state
# configurations, which for some elements differ from Madelung filling -- see
# slater._CONFIG_EXCEPTIONS (e.g. Pd has no 5s entry here because its ground state is 4d10).
# Coverage ends at Z=54 (Xe); heavier elements fall back to Slater's rules (slater.z_eff).

